export const terms = "> **DRAFT — NOT YET IN EFFECT. Needs attorney review before AgsSwap launches.** Adapted from the RenoSwap documents for farm & ranch use. Items marked **[REVIEW]** especially need a lawyer's eyes.\n\n**Effective date:** TBD (draft) · **Version:** 1.0-draft\n\n## 1. Who we are and what these terms cover\n\nAgsSwap (\"AgsSwap,\" \"we,\" \"us\"), a RenoSwap company, is run by RenoSwap LLC, a Texas limited liability company doing business as AgsSwap. **[REVIEW: confirm the assumed-name (DBA) filing, or replace with a separate AgsSwap LLC if one is formed.]** AgsSwap is a website that helps people swap, sell, or give away farm and ranch equipment, supplies, hay, and livestock.\n\nThese Terms of Service (\"Terms\") are a contract between you and us. They cover your use of agsswap.com, agsswap.vercel.app, and any other AgsSwap site or app (together, the \"Service\"). By creating an account or using the Service, you agree to these Terms, our [Privacy Policy](/privacy), and our [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited). If you don't agree, please don't use AgsSwap.\n\n## 2. Who can use AgsSwap\n\n- You must be **18 or older**.\n- You must give us accurate information and keep it up to date.\n- One person per account. Keep your password private. You're responsible for what happens under your account.\n- If you use AgsSwap for a business (for example, a ranch, farm, or feed store), you confirm you're allowed to act for that business, and these Terms apply to the business too.\n- AgsSwap is based in Texas and starts with Texas, but is open across the United States. Listings need a valid U.S. ZIP code.\n\n## 3. What AgsSwap does, and doesn't do\n\nAgsSwap is **only a venue**: a place for users to connect. We are **not** a party to any swap, sale, or giveaway between users, we are not a buyer, seller, broker, or agent, and we are **not responsible or liable for meetups, pickups, or deliveries** between users.\n\n- **We don't handle payment for items or animals.** Buyers and sellers arrange payment (cash, Venmo, Zelle, etc.) and pickup or shipping themselves. AgsSwap never holds money for items or animals and takes no cut of sales.\n- **We don't inspect, test, store, or deliver items, and we don't guarantee them.** We don't guarantee that any item is as described, safe, healthy, sound, legal, or fit for your purpose. We don't check animal health, brands, titles, or ownership papers.\n- **We don't check users' backgrounds.** A \"Ranch / Farm\" label means the user says they run a ranch or farm or is on the Ranch / Farm plan. It is **not** a license check, brand check, or endorsement.\n- **Admin review is limited.** An admin looks at listings before they go public. That review is a quick check against our rules, not an inspection or a promise that the listing is accurate or lawful.\n\nYou deal with other users at your own risk. Use good judgment and read our [safety tips](/safety).\n\n## 4. Listings\n\n**Listing types.** You can list items as:\n\n- **Swap:** trade for other items.\n- **Sell:** for a price you set.\n- **Sell or Swap:** either one.\n- **Fast & Free:** a free giveaway with a pickup timer. The timer starts when an admin approves the listing, and the listing expires when the timer runs out.\n\n**Your promises when you list.** You promise that:\n\n- You own the item or have the right to give or sell it. For livestock, that means you own the animals (and any brand on them is yours or properly transferred to you). For titled trailers and vehicles, it means you hold the title or can sign it over.\n- Your description and photos are honest and are photos of the actual item. You disclose known defects, damage, age, and anything a reasonable person would want to know, such as hours on equipment, hydraulic leaks, frame damage, hay cutting and storage, and for animals: age, sex, breed, known health problems, vaccinations, and whether they're bred.\n- The item isn't on our [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited) and isn't illegal to sell or give away.\n- Listings are for **physical goods and livestock**, not services (like custom hay baling, fence building, hauling, stud service, or day labor), job ads, or ads for other businesses.\n\n**Livestock listings. [REVIEW]** If you list animals, you also promise that:\n\n- The animals are healthy to the best of your knowledge, aren't under a quarantine or hold order, and you'll disclose any known illness, injury, or treatment withdrawal times.\n- You'll follow Texas Animal Health Commission and federal animal-movement rules that apply, such as official ID or tags, health certificates, negative Coggins (EIA) tests for horses, and scrapie tags for sheep and goats, where required.\n- You'll handle brand transfer and any bill of sale yourself. AgsSwap doesn't inspect brands or record ownership.\n- The buyer is responsible for the animal's care, transport, and health once it leaves your place.\n\n**Our rights.** We can refuse, edit the display of, pause, expire, or remove any listing at any time, for any reason or no reason, including after it was approved. Non-free listings may expire after about 45 days.\n\n**Distance.** Browse shows an **approximate** distance (for example, \"~12 mi\") calculated from ZIP codes, not exact addresses. It's an estimate only; confirm the pickup location with the other user.\n\n**Photos.** When you upload a photo, the app removes GPS location data stored in the image file. Still, don't photograph anything that shows your address.\n\n**Deals.** An offer or message on AgsSwap is not a binding contract with us. Any deal is only between you and the other user.\n\n## 5. Messages, offers, and reports\n\n- Use messages and offers only to talk about listings. No spam, harassment, threats, hate, or scams.\n- Don't ask for or share sensitive information like bank logins, Social Security numbers, or ID photos.\n- You can **report** a listing or user. Reports go to our admins, who decide what to do.\n- To keep people safe and enforce these Terms, our admins **can read messages, offers, and reports** when needed (for example, when something is reported). See the [Privacy Policy](/privacy).\n\n**Ratings and reviews.** After both users confirm a trade, each can leave a 1–5 star rating and an optional comment. Reviews must be honest and about that trade. Don't fake trades to boost ratings. We may hide or remove reviews that break these Terms.\n\n**Email alerts.** We email you about new offers and messages and, if you set them up, \"Looking for\" alerts when matching listings are approved. You can turn these off on the Account page or with the unsubscribe link in any alert email. We'll still send required account emails (like sign-up confirmations and password resets).\n\n## 6. Plans, payments, and refunds\n\n**Free plan.** Up to **3 active listings** (active means pending review, approved, or claimed).\n\n**Paid plans (monthly subscriptions):**\n\n| Plan | Price | Active listings |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hobby farm | $4.99/month | up to 10 |\n| Ranch / Farm | $19.99/month | up to 25, plus a Ranch / Farm badge |\n\n**Listing boost:** **$1.99 one-time** per listing. A boosted listing is shown near the top of Browse for **7 days**.\n\n- **Payments are processed by Stripe.** We never see or store your full card number. Stripe's own terms and privacy policy also apply.\n- **Subscriptions renew automatically every month** until you cancel. By subscribing, you authorize us (through Stripe) to charge your payment method each month.\n- **Switching plans.** If you switch between Hobby farm and Ranch / Farm, Stripe adjusts the charge for the rest of the month (a prorated credit or charge).\n- **Canceling.** Cancel anytime from **Billing → Manage billing**. Your plan stays active until the end of the period you already paid for, then returns to Free. If you then have more active listings than the Free plan allows, your existing listings aren't deleted, but you can't post new ones until you're under the limit.\n- **Refunds.** Payments are **non-refundable**, including partial months, **unless the law requires a refund**. Boosts are **non-refundable once applied**. If we remove your boosted listing for breaking our rules, you don't get a refund. If we make a billing mistake, contact us and we'll fix it.\n- **Price changes.** We may change prices. We'll tell you at least 30 days before a new price applies to your subscription, and you can cancel before then.\n- **Taxes.** Prices may not include applicable sales tax. If tax applies, it will be shown at checkout.\n- **Failed payments.** If a payment fails, your paid plan may end and your account goes back to Free.\n\n## 7. Your content\n\n\"Your content\" means your listings, photos, profile (name, photo, bio, ranch or farm name, city), messages, and reports.\n\n- You keep ownership of your content.\n- You give us a **non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide license** to host, store, copy, resize, display, and share your content to run, improve, and promote AgsSwap (for example, showing your listing on Browse or in a social media post about AgsSwap). This license ends when you delete the content or your account, except for copies we reasonably keep for backups, legal reasons, or safety records, and content already shared with other users (like messages you sent).\n- You promise you have the rights to what you upload (for example, you took the photos) and that it doesn't break the law or anyone's rights.\n- Don't post other people's personal information.\n\n## 8. Rules of conduct\n\nDon't:\n\n- Break the law or help anyone else break it.\n- List or trade anything on the [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited).\n- Post fake, misleading, duplicate, or bait-and-switch listings, or use AgsSwap to advertise off-site sales or services.\n- Scam, harass, threaten, discriminate against, or impersonate anyone.\n- Get around listing limits (for example, with multiple accounts) or misuse boosts, reports, or payments.\n- Scrape, copy, or collect data about users, or send spam.\n- Hack, overload, reverse-engineer, or interfere with the Service or its security.\n\n## 9. Suspension and ending your account\n\n- **You** can stop using AgsSwap anytime. To delete your account, use **Delete account** at the bottom of the **Account** page (or email hello@agsswap.com). Cancel any paid plan first (see Section 6). Deleting your account removes your listings, photos, alerts, and settings; people you messaged keep the conversation, shown as from a \"Deleted member.\"\n- **We** can suspend or close your account, remove content, or limit features at any time if we believe you broke these Terms, created risk or legal exposure, or to protect users. We'll try to tell you why, unless the law or safety reasons prevent it. If we close your account for breaking these Terms, you don't get a refund.\n- Sections that should survive after your account ends will (for example, Sections 7, 10–14).\n\n## 10. Disclaimers\n\nAgsSwap is provided **\"as is\" and \"as available.\"** To the fullest extent the law allows, we make **no warranties** of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and non-infringement. We don't promise that the Service will always be available, error-free, or secure, or that any user, listing, or item is safe, legal, accurate, or as described.\n\nFarm equipment, trailers, and livestock can be heavy, powerful, and dangerous. Animals can kick, bite, carry disease, or get sick after a move. **You are responsible** for inspecting items and animals (or having a veterinarian or mechanic do it), following safety rules and animal-health laws, and loading, hauling, and handling everything properly.\n\n## 11. Limit on our liability\n\nTo the fullest extent the law allows:\n\n- We are **not liable** for anything that happens between users, including items, animals, animal health, payments, meetups, pickups, hauling, injuries, property damage, or disputes.\n- We are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or lost profits, data, or goodwill.\n- Our **total liability** for any claim related to AgsSwap is limited to the **greater of $100 or the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim**.\n\nSome laws don't allow some of these limits. If so, they apply only as far as the law allows.\n\n## 12. Disputes between users; your promise to cover us\n\n- **Disputes between users are between those users.** You release RenoSwap LLC and its owners, employees, and agents from claims arising from your dealings with other users, to the extent the law allows. We may, but don't have to, help.\n- **Indemnity.** You agree to defend and cover us (including reasonable attorney fees) against claims from others that come from your content, your listings or deals, your breaking these Terms, or your breaking the law.\n\n## 13. Disputes with AgsSwap\n\n- **Talk to us first.** Please email hello@agsswap.com with your concern. Most problems can be solved quickly. Give us 30 days to try to resolve it before filing a claim.\n- **Texas law.** These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules.\n- **Where cases go.** Any lawsuit must be brought in the state or federal courts located in **Lavaca County, Texas**. Either of us may instead bring an eligible claim in **small claims court (justice court)** in the Texas county where you live or in Lavaca County.\n- **No arbitration.** These Terms don't require arbitration.\n\n## 14. Other terms\n\n- **Changes.** We may update these Terms. If a change is significant, we'll let you know (for example, by email or a notice on the site) before it takes effect. If you keep using AgsSwap after that, you accept the new Terms. We may ask you to agree again.\n- **Whole agreement.** These Terms, the Privacy Policy, and the Prohibited Items list are the whole agreement between you and us about AgsSwap.\n- **If a part is invalid,** the rest still applies.\n- **Not giving up rights.** If we don't enforce something right away, we can still enforce it later.\n- **Transfer.** You can't transfer your account or these Terms. We may transfer them, for example if AgsSwap is sold or moved to a separate company.\n- **Events outside our control.** We're not responsible for delays or failures caused by things we can't reasonably control, like outages at our service providers, storms, drought, wildfire, or power failures.\n\n## 15. Contact\n\nRenoSwap LLC (d/b/a AgsSwap, a RenoSwap company)\n404 W McKinney St, Moulton, TX 77975-5008\nhello@agsswap.com\n";
export const privacy = "> **DRAFT — NOT YET IN EFFECT. Needs attorney review before AgsSwap launches.** Adapted from the RenoSwap documents for farm & ranch use. Items marked **[REVIEW]** especially need a lawyer's eyes.\n\n**Effective date:** TBD (draft) · **Version:** 1.0-draft\n\nThis policy explains what information AgsSwap collects, how we use it, who can see it, and your choices. AgsSwap, a RenoSwap company, is run by RenoSwap LLC (\"we,\" \"us\").\n\n**The short version:** we collect what we need to run a local farm & ranch marketplace. **We don't sell your personal information, and we don't show ads.** Your profile and listings are public. Your messages are private between you and the other person, but our admins can read them to keep people safe. Card details are handled by Stripe, not us.\n\n## 1. What we collect\n\n**Information you give us:**\n\n- **Account:** email address and password. Your password is handled by our login provider (Supabase Auth) and stored in a scrambled (hashed) form. We can't see it.\n- **Profile:** display name, role (Hobby farm or Ranch / Farm), ranch or farm name (if you add one), city, ZIP code, a short bio, and a profile photo (optional).\n- **Listings:** title, category, condition, description, what you're looking for in a swap, price, city and ZIP, pickup/shipping options, the listing type (Swap, Sell, Sell or Swap, Fast & Free), and photos.\n- **Messages and offers** you send to other users.\n- **Reports** you file about listings or users, including your reason and details.\n- **Trades, ratings, and reviews:** trades you mark complete or confirm, star ratings and comments you leave, and reports about reviews.\n- **Alerts and email settings:** your \"Looking for\" alerts and whether offer, message, and alert emails are on or off.\n- **Support emails** you send us.\n\n**Billing information:**\n\n- If you buy a plan or a boost, **Stripe** collects your payment card and billing details. **We never receive or store your full card number.**\n- We keep your billing status: your plan, whether it's active, when it renews or ends, a Stripe customer ID, and which listings you boosted.\n\n**Information collected automatically:**\n\n- **Login cookies.** We use a small number of cookies to keep you signed in and secure your session. We **don't** use advertising or tracking cookies.\n- **Basic logs.** Our hosting and database providers automatically record technical information like IP address, browser type, pages requested, and the time, for security and to fix problems.\n\nWe don't currently send browser push notifications, and we don't collect your precise location. We only know the city and ZIP you type in. **Distance on Browse is approximate**: we estimate it from ZIP codes (for example, \"~12 mi\") and never show your address. **Photos:** when you upload a photo, the app strips GPS location data from the image file before it's stored.\n\n## 2. What's public and what's private\n\n**Public (anyone, even without an account, can see):**\n\n- Your **display name, profile photo, city, bio, ranch or farm name, and Ranch / Farm label**\n- Your **approved listings**, including photos, description, price, and **city and ZIP**\n- Your **star rating and reviews** from completed trades (reviews appear once both people have left one, or after 7 days)\n\nOnly put in your profile and listings what you're comfortable sharing publicly. **Don't put your street address or phone number in a listing.** Share those in private messages only when you're ready.\n\n**Private:**\n\n- **Your email address** isn't shown on the site. *(See the note for the owner at the end of this document.)*\n- **Messages and offers** can only be seen by the people in the conversation and by **AgsSwap admins**. Admins may review them to check reports, stop scams or abuse, or enforce our Terms.\n- **Reports** can only be seen by the person who filed them and by admins.\n- **Billing details** are only visible to you, our admins, and Stripe.\n\n## 3. How we use your information\n\n- To create and run your account, and to show your profile and listings\n- To review and approve listings, and to handle reports\n- To let you message other users and make offers\n- To process subscriptions and boosts (through Stripe) and apply your plan's listing limits\n- To send account emails, like sign-up confirmations and password resets, and important notices about your account or policy changes\n- To send **email alerts** you can control: new offers and messages, and \"Looking for\" matches. Every alert email has an **unsubscribe** link, and you can turn alerts on or off on the Account page\n- To keep AgsSwap safe: preventing fraud, spam, and abuse, and enforcing our Terms\n- To fix bugs and improve the Service\n- To follow the law and respond to valid legal requests\n\nWe don't send marketing emails without your permission. We don't use your information for advertising.\n\n## 4. Who we share it with\n\n**We don't sell or rent your personal information.** We share it only:\n\n- **With other users**, as described in Section 2\n- **With service providers** that run AgsSwap for us, only as needed to provide their services:\n  - **Supabase:** database, login, and file storage (profiles, listings, photos, messages)\n  - **Vercel:** website hosting (and the basic logs described above)\n  - **Stripe:** payments and billing\n  - **Resend:** sends account emails and email alerts\n- **For legal reasons:** if the law requires it, to respond to valid legal requests, or to protect the rights, safety, or property of our users, the public, or AgsSwap\n- **If the business changes hands:** if AgsSwap is sold or merged, your information may transfer to the new owner, who must follow this policy or tell you about changes\n\nOur providers may store data on servers outside Texas, including elsewhere in the United States.\n\n## 5. How long we keep it\n\n- We keep account, profile, and listing information while your account is open.\n- Rejected or expired listings may stay in our records so admins can review history.\n- When you delete your account, we delete your profile, listings, photos, alerts, and settings right away. Messages you sent stay visible to the other person, shown as from a \"Deleted member,\" and remaining records are deleted or de-identified, usually within **30 days**. Some things may stay longer:\n  - copies in backups, until they expire\n  - billing and payment records we must keep for tax and accounting\n  - records of reports or rule violations kept for safety\n  - messages you sent may still be visible to the other person if they're kept for a report\n- Hosting and database logs are kept for a limited time by our providers.\n\n## 6. Your choices and rights\n\n- **Edit your profile** anytime on the Account page, including adding, changing, or removing your photo.\n- **Edit or remove listings** from My listings, or ask us to remove them.\n- **Cancel a plan** from Billing → Manage billing.\n- **Delete your account** yourself anytime: tap **Delete account** at the bottom of the Account page and type DELETE to confirm. Or email hello@agsswap.com from the email address on your account.\n- **Turn email alerts off** on the Account page, or use the unsubscribe link in any alert email.\n- **Get a copy or correct your information:** email us and we'll help.\n\nDepending on where you live, you may have additional privacy rights. Contact us and we'll respond as the law requires. We won't treat you differently for using your privacy rights.\n\n## 7. Security\n\nWe use reasonable safeguards: encrypted connections (HTTPS), hashed passwords, database access rules that limit who can see what, and trusted providers. No website is perfectly secure, so use a strong, unique password and tell us right away if you think your account was misused.\n\n## 8. Age limit\n\nAgsSwap is for adults **18 and older**. We don't knowingly collect information from children under 13. If you think a child has given us information, contact us and we'll delete it.\n\n## 9. Changes to this policy\n\nIf we make significant changes, we'll let you know (for example, by email or a notice on the site) before they take effect. The date at the top shows the latest version.\n\n## 10. Contact\n\nRenoSwap LLC (d/b/a AgsSwap)\n404 W McKinney St, Moulton, TX 77975-5008\nhello@agsswap.com\n";
export const prohibited = "> **DRAFT — NOT YET IN EFFECT. Needs attorney review before AgsSwap launches.** Adapted from the RenoSwap Prohibited Items list for farm & ranch use. Items marked **[REVIEW]** especially need a lawyer's eyes.\n\n**Effective date:** TBD (draft)\n\nAgsSwap is for **farm and ranch equipment, supplies, hay and forage, and livestock**. Most things you'd find around a working place are fine to list: tractors and implements, fencing, panels and gates, trailers, tack, stock tanks, hay, sealed feed, and healthy animals. But some things are dangerous, illegal, or need a license. **Don't list the items below.** Admins will reject or remove them, and repeat or serious violations can get your account closed.\n\nThis list isn't complete. If something is illegal to sell or give away in Texas or under federal law, it's not allowed even if it's not listed here. When in doubt, leave it out, or email hello@agsswap.com and ask.\n\n## Firearms, weapons, and explosives\n\n- **Firearms of any kind**, including rifles, shotguns, handguns, antique guns, air guns used as firearms, receivers, frames, and gun parts kits.\n- **Ammunition**, reloading powder and primers, magazines, suppressors, and bump stocks.\n- **Explosives**: blasting supplies, binary exploding targets, fireworks, and stump-removal explosives.\n- Switchblades, brass knuckles, and other weapons that are illegal to sell where you or the buyer live.\n\n## Pesticides, chemicals, and fertilizers\n\n- **Restricted-use pesticides**, and any pesticide or herbicide that requires an applicator license to buy or use. **[REVIEW]**\n- **Opened, partly used, unlabeled, or repackaged** pesticides, herbicides, insecticides, rodenticides, fly baits, and dewormers.\n- **Anhydrous ammonia**, **ammonium nitrate** fertilizer, and other fertilizers regulated as explosive precursors.\n- Fuel and gas: gasoline, diesel, kerosene, and **propane or other gas cylinders**. Empty fuel tanks and transfer tanks must be clearly described as empty and purged.\n- Refrigerants, open solvents, acids, and other hazardous chemicals in anything other than their sealed original container.\n- Used motor oil, hydraulic fluid, antifreeze, and other waste fluids.\n\n## Animal health products and food\n\n- **Prescription and veterinary-only drugs**, including antibiotics that need a veterinarian's order, **Veterinary Feed Directive (VFD)** feeds, vaccines that require refrigeration and a cold chain, and any controlled substance. **[REVIEW]**\n- Used needles, syringes, and other sharps.\n- **Food for people**: raw milk, home-processed meat, eggs, honey, canned goods, and baked goods. **[REVIEW: Texas cottage food and egg-sale rules.]**\n- **Opened or contaminated feed**, medicated feed, and feed that has been wet, moldy, or exposed to chemicals.\n\n## Livestock and animals\n\nHealthy livestock is welcome in the **Livestock** category. These are **not** allowed:\n\n- **Sick, injured, or diseased animals**, or animals from a herd or flock under a **quarantine or hold order**.\n- Animals that can't legally change hands without paperwork you don't have, such as horses without a current negative **Coggins (EIA) test**, or sheep and goats without required **scrapie** ID, where those are required. **[REVIEW: Texas Animal Health Commission rules.]**\n- **Wildlife**: native game animals and birds, venomous reptiles, endangered or protected species, and animals that need a state or federal permit you can't transfer. **[REVIEW: exotic hoofstock rules.]**\n- **Dogs, cats, and other pets.** Working stock dogs are not allowed in this first version. **[REVIEW]**\n- Animals for fighting, and any fighting gear (for example, gaffs and spurs for cockfighting).\n- Unweaned young animals offered without their mother, except bottle calves, kids, or lambs clearly described as bottle babies.\n- Animal parts protected by law, such as eagle and other migratory-bird feathers.\n\n## Seeds, plants, and hay\n\n- **Unlabeled seed for planting** that you're selling (giveaways of saved garden seed are OK if clearly described as saved seed). **[REVIEW: Texas seed law.]**\n- **Noxious or invasive plants and weed seed**, and plants under a **quarantine** (for example, citrus nursery stock in quarantine areas).\n- Hay must be honestly described. Don't hide mold, weeds, or blister-beetle risk in alfalfa.\n\n## Equipment, trailers, and vehicles\n\n- **Stolen equipment**, livestock, trailers, or tools, or anything you don't have the right to sell or give away.\n- Items with **serial numbers, VINs, or PINs removed or altered**.\n- Titled trailers and vehicles **without a title** you can sign over (salvage and parts-only items must say so).\n- **Catalytic converters** and other items covered by Texas metal-recycling and theft rules. **[REVIEW]**\n- **Recalled products**, such as heaters, chainsaws, or ladders. Check before listing at **[CPSC.gov/Recalls](https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls)**.\n- Equipment with known dangerous defects (failed brakes, cracked hitch, missing PTO shields) unless it's clearly listed as **parts / salvage** and the defect is described.\n\n## Treated wood and building leftovers **[REVIEW]**\n\n- Used **railroad ties** and **utility poles** (creosote-treated) may be listed only for fencing or corral use and must be clearly described as used treated wood. Don't market them for gardens, raised beds, or anywhere near food or water for animals.\n- Asbestos-containing materials, lead-paint debris, and moldy or flood-damaged building materials aren't allowed.\n\n## Always-prohibited items\n\n- Illegal drugs and drug paraphernalia; alcohol; tobacco and vape products; human prescription medicines\n- **Counterfeit** or knock-off branded goods\n- Anything else that's illegal to sell, give away, or own\n\n## Not allowed as listings\n\n- **Services instead of goods**: custom baling, shredding, fence building, hauling, stud or breeding service, boarding, day labor, or job postings. Equipment, supplies, and animals are fine to list.\n- **Land, leases, or hunting leases.** **[REVIEW]**\n- **Spam, fake, or misleading listings**, including stock photos, bait-and-switch prices, duplicate posts, or \"contact me off-site for a better deal.\"\n- **Ads for another business or website**, or listings that just collect contact information.\n- **Trash or junk dumping**: things no one could reasonably reuse. (It's fine to mark reusable items \"Headed for scrap\" to get them rescued.)\n- Listings that include someone else's personal information, or offensive, hateful, or adult content.\n- Anything that breaks our [Terms of Service](/terms) or the law.\n\nBefore you meet up, read our [safety tips](/safety).\n";
export const safety = "> **DRAFT — NOT YET IN EFFECT. Needs attorney review before AgsSwap launches.** Adapted from the RenoSwap safety tips for farm & ranch use.\n\n**Effective date:** TBD (draft)\n\nAgsSwap doesn't handle payment, pickups, or hauling, so a little caution goes a long way.\n\n**Before you meet**\n\n- Keep talking in AgsSwap messages until you're ready to meet, so there's a record if something goes wrong.\n- Ask for extra photos, video of equipment running, hour-meter readings, and for animals, recent records (vaccinations, Coggins, health papers). Confirm the quantity, condition, and price before you drive out.\n- **Never pay in advance** to someone you haven't met. Avoid wire transfers, gift cards, crypto, and \"I'll overpay, send me the difference\" offers. Those are common scams, especially with livestock, puppies, and horses that \"just need shipping.\"\n- Don't share your gate code or exact location until you're ready to arrange pickup.\n\n**Meeting up**\n\n- For small items, meet in a **public, well-lit place** during the day, like a feed store or sale barn parking lot, or a police station \"safe exchange\" spot.\n- For equipment, hay, and animals that need a ranch pickup, **have someone with you**, tell a friend where you're going, and go in daylight.\n- Trust your gut. If something feels off, leave.\n\n**Inspecting**\n\n- Look items over before you pay: hydraulics, tires, welds, hitch and safety chains, wiring, and rust-through on trailers.\n- For hay, check for mold, heat, weeds, and moisture. For alfalfa, ask about blister beetles.\n- For animals, watch them move, check eyes, nose, feet, and body condition, and **ask your veterinarian** before buying. Keep new animals apart from your herd until you know they're healthy.\n- Make sure brands, bills of sale, and titles match the person selling.\n\n**Paying**\n\n- Use a payment method you trust, and **only pay once you have the item or animal**. Cash is simple. With payment apps, be sure you know who you're paying.\n- Write a simple **bill of sale** for animals, trailers, and equipment.\n\n**Loading and hauling**\n\n- Bring the right trailer, straps, chains, and a helper. Know your truck's towing and tongue-weight limits.\n- Keep clear of PTO shafts, three-point hitches, and raised loaders. Never stand between a tractor and an implement while hitching.\n- Load animals calmly with proper panels or a chute, and haul them with enough space, ventilation, and water.\n- In Texas heat, bring water, haul animals in the cooler part of the day, and don't overdo heavy lifting.\n\n**If something goes wrong**\n\n- Use **Report** on the listing or user, and email hello@agsswap.com.\n- For suspected livestock or equipment theft, contact your county sheriff and the **Texas & Southwestern Cattle Raisers Association** special rangers.\n- If you're in danger or a crime has happened, call **911** or your local police.\n\nRead the [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited) and [Terms of Service](/terms). AgsSwap is only a venue, isn't part of any deal, and isn't liable for meetups, hauling, or animal health.\n";
